    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian-British Association (IBA) requires a consignment bilty that documents the cargo’s origin, destination, weight, and handling instructions. This bilty serves as a transport contract and is essential for customs and liability purposes.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>In addition to these documents, you should consider the <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong>. This specialized policy guarantees that the full declared value of your vehicle is covered against loss, damage, or theft during the marine segment of the journey.</p>
<p>It offers peace of mind, especially when navigating the complex coastal routes and potential hazards associated with sea transport. The insurance is typically structured as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Coverage Limit</strong> – Equal to the vehicle’s market value at the time of shipping.</li>
<li><strong>Risk Coverage</strong> – Includes collision, theft, fire, and accidental damage.</li>
<li><strong>Claims Process</strong> – Fast-track claims with a dedicated marine insurance broker.</li>
</ul>
<p>By ensuring you have all these documents in order and opting for 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance, you can confidently transport your vehicle from Delhi to Srinagar, knowing that every legal, regulatory, and safety requirement is fully met.</p></div>
